WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:08.812
In the Encyclopedia of Triangle Centers, the O I Line is the central axis joining the Incenter X one and the Circumcenter X three.

2
00:00:08.812 --> 00:00:15.010
By Euler's formula, the squared distance between X one and X three equals R times R minus two r.

3
00:00:15.430 --> 00:00:26.383
Because the incircle and circumcircle are centered at X one and X three, both of their centers of similitude—the insimilicenter X fifty-five and exsimilicenter X fifty-six—lie on the O I line.

4
00:00:26.383 --> 00:00:33.400
Furthermore, the reflection of X one across X three is the Bevan Point X forty, the circumcenter of the excentral triangle.

5
00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:45.340
Through isogonal conjugation, the Gergonne Point X seven pairs with X fifty-five and the Nagel Point X eight pairs with X fifty-seven on the O I line, uniting the tritangent and circumcircle geometries.
